  "version": 1,
  "title": "B-final sibling phrase bank — pt / el / living Latin-derived shorts",
  "notes": [
    "Additive sibling to zh_de_phrases.json (does not rewrite ZH/DE/EN/JA entries).",
    "Living Portuguese, modern Greek, Italian, and surviving scholarly Latin only.",
    "Classical Latin conjugations live in es_fr_tense.json candidates only when they win tokens and pass AI round-trip (veniam); surviving Latin abbrevs like e.g./i.e./etc. stay C.",
    "Only forms that beat the English source on estimate_tokens; runtime cheapest (token→utf8→len).",
    "No hyphen morphology. Compound-style multiword EN → short densifier is a candidate class, not noun-only.",
    "Country-only jargon (CTT, BI) and sense-lossy truncations are in examples_not_registered.",
    "la (<100M speakers): every la form must pass AI round-trip exact-match ≥0.9 (roundtrip.json; judge answers in roundtrip_judge/la_blind.json). The 9 pre-gate la shorts that restored to a synonym (iterum, ergo, circa, coram, cotidie/quotidie, ideo, pro, re, inter alia←among others) were reversed; gradatim kept."
